{"id":"fdf3db0e-8a99-43c4-abcb-07104fba4427","object":"chat.completion","created":1795243706,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"SELECT c.customer_state,\n       ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE r.review_score BETWEEN 1 AND 2) / COUNT(*), 2) AS low_rating_pct\nFROM order_reviews r\nJOIN orders o ON o.order_id = r.order_id\nJOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\nWHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled', 'unavailable')\nGROUP BY c.customer_state\nORDER BY low_rating_pct DESC, c.customer_state ASC\nLIMIT 10;","reasoning_content":"We need answer only SQL. Need parse. Need produce SELECT one query LIMIT. Need use valid_order filter. Question: \"按订单客户档案所在州统计有效订单评价记录中1到2星评价占比百分数两位，每条评价等权；按比例取前10，同值按州升序，仅输出州和比例。\"\n\nNeed compute for valid orders (order_status not canceled/unavailable), review records from order_reviews joined orders customers. Each review equal weight (so count review rows, not orders). Group by customer_state from order's customer record (customers.customer_id = o.customer_id). Percentage low scores <=2? \"1到2星评价\" = review_score between 1 and 2. Percentage = 100.0*count filter / count(*) two decimals. Top 10 by proportion desc, same state asc. Output state and ratio only.\n\nNeed consider state maybe NULL? For top by ratio, if all? Use ORDER BY pct DESC, state ASC LIMIT 10. Need maybe alias. The reference example filters valid. Count each review row. Since order_reviews primary key combination review_id, order_id; multiple reviews per order possible maybe each row. \"每条评价等权\" means count rows. JOIN orders and customers. Could customer duplicates? customers PK customer_id so each order customer one customer record. Good. order_reviews may have same order multiple reviews; each counted. Could reviews for invalid orders excluded by WHERE. Need not filter review_score null? \"评价记录中1到2星评价占比\" All review records? If review_score NULL, not low but denominator includes? 1-2 stars numerator. Usually review_score likely nonnull. We should not add non-null filter unless requested. The \"评价记录\" includes rows, even if score null? hmm. Could be unknown. But no explicit \"仅评分非空\". Rule no unauth filters. So COUNT(*) all review rows for valid orders. Numerator FILTER (review_score BETWEEN 1 AND 2) — NULL false. Good.\n\nOutput percentage two decimals. Need ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(*) FILTER(...) / COUNT(*), 2). Since COUNT ints and 100.0 numeric? 100.0 numeric, expression numeric. Good.\n\nNeed alias maybe low_rating_pct. \"仅输出州和比例\" state and pct. Alias okay. Use c.customer_state as state? Could alias state? They requested only columns. If use customer_state, low_pct. Query:\n\nSELECT c.customer_state,\n       ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE r.review_score BETWEEN 1 AND 2) / COUNT(*), 2) AS low_rating_pct\nFROM order_reviews r\nJOIN orders o ON o.order_id = r.order_id\nJOIN customers c ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\nWHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled','unavailable')\nGROUP BY c.customer_state\nORDER BY low_rating_pct DESC, c.customer_state ASC\nLIMIT 10;\n\nNeed potential issue \"按比例取前10，同值按州升序\". We used rounded pct for ordering? Rule says by final display precision rank/equality. Yes use alias pct (rounded) likely. PostgreSQL alias in ORDER BY allowed. Same-value tie by state. Good.\n\nNeed ensure only SELECT. No code fences. final only SQL. \n"},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3706,"completion_tokens":842,"total_tokens":4548,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":721},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1792,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1914},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}